'' A UDT COMPARED WITH A POINTER takes its pointer 'operator cast' -- the exact one for that
'' pointer, else the 'any ptr' one (PtrCastPick). fbc-modern 1.20 prints these eight lines
'' (2026-11-13); tiko handed the object itself to icmp and stopped on TKO0993 ("an operand
'' with no kind"). udt-ptr-compare.test has the comparisons fbc refuses.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-ptr-cast-compare.bas -o tests/codegen/udtptrcastcmp.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udtptrcastcmp.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 4-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 5-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 6 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 7-1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 8 0
